    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Independent since 1818, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/army-of-the-andes">Army of the Andes</a> defeated the royalists at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chacabuco">Chacabuco</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-maipu">Maipú</a>.</li><li>The Constitution of 1833 gave it rare stability, and victory in the War of the Pacific made it a regional power.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador-allende">Salvador Allende</a> was overthrown in 1973; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augusto-pinochet">Pinochet</a>’s dictatorship lasted until the return of democracy in 1990.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andres-bello">Andrés Bello</a>, a Venezuelan scholar who settled in Chile, wrote its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chilean-civil-code">Civil Code of 1855</a>, which was later adopted by Ecuador and Colombia.</p></aside>
    </section>

